{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f07e39d99b57bc5afd", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Ray Optics - Test 1", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dced7"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce8e", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce23", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3b"], "concepts": ["6162fb466ed13040ec84d05a"], "question": {"text": "When one light ray is reflected from a plane mirror with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> angle of reflection, the angle of deviation of the ray after reflection is:"}, "options": [{"id": "85247a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce24"}, {"id": "75839e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>110</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce25"}, {"id": "56f924", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>140</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce26"}, {"id": "894ba8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>130</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce27"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce28", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f39"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c2"], "question": {"text": "A concave mirror of focal length $f$ in air is dipped in a liquid of refractive index $\\mu$. Its focal length in the liquid will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "cad87b", "text": "$\\mu f$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce29"}, {"id": "f2cf71", "text": "$f$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce2a"}, {"id": "fdd5b3", "text": "$\\frac{f}{(\\mu-1)}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce2b"}, {"id": "33965d", "text": "$\\frac{f}{\\mu}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce2c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce2d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4756"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8eda"], "question": {"text": "The critical angle of a medium for a specific wavelength, if the medium has relative permittivity <math><mn>3</mn></math> and relative permeability <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> for this wavelength, will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "7f4483", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce2e"}, {"id": "39ccd6", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce2f"}, {"id": "1ede9c", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce30"}, {"id": "3ba972", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce31"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce32", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b4f"], "question": {"text": "The difference of speed of light in the two media <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If the refractive index of medium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>47</mn></math>, then the ratio of refractive index of medium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to medium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is: (Given : speed of light in vacuum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "b15c65", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce33"}, {"id": "c84c77", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>318</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce34"}, {"id": "42d75c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>13</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce35"}, {"id": "bbafb7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce36"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce37", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9250"], "question": {"text": "<p>The graph shows how the magnification <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> produced by a thin lens varies with image distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. The focal length of the lens used is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F16b1576e-b82d-4b00-8a63-570c0674cb95-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 239px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "00817f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce38"}, {"id": "e05468", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce39"}, {"id": "a93c2e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce3a"}, {"id": "cf44e4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce3b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce3c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538326"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f925c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The angle of deviation through a prism is minimum when&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fcbc0fa84-a47d-40f7-beb8-f02a05981a07-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 291px; height: 164px;\" /></p><p>(A) Incident ray and emergent ray are symmetric to the prism</p><p>(B) The refracted ray inside the prism becomes parallel to its base</p><p>(C) Angle of incidence is equal to that of the angle of emergence</p><p>(D) When angle of emergence is double the angle of incidence</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2dfcbe", "text": "Statements (A),(B)&nbsp;and (C)&nbsp;are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce3d"}, {"id": "7e3f19", "text": "Only statement (D) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce3e"}, {"id": "88157c", "text": "Only statements (A) and (B) are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce3f"}, {"id": "906165", "text": "Statements (B) and (C) are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce40"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce41", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b474f"], "concepts": ["60da9b4f62f042332c5382ed"], "question": {"text": "The magnifying power of a telescope with tube length <math><mn>60</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is <math><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo></math> What is the focal length of its eye piece?"}, "options": [{"id": "cec0cc", "text": "<math><mn>20</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce42"}, {"id": "89c9a4", "text": "<math><mn>40</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce43"}, {"id": "131d5e", "text": "<math><mn>30</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce44"}, {"id": "8a870f", "text": "<math><mn>10</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce45"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce46", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["6176f3f86581241c7072b2e2"], "concepts": ["617aa9daef3fe65ad8e829e8"], "question": {"text": "Your friend is having eye sight problem. She is not able to see clearly a distant uniform window mesh and it appears to her as nonuniform and distorted. The doctor diagnosed the problem as :"}, "options": [{"id": "eda639", "text": "Astigmatism", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce47"}, {"id": "a806e9", "text": "Myopia with Astigmatism", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce48"}, {"id": "4a7774", "text": "Presbyopia with Astigmatism", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce49"}, {"id": "dfb713", "text": "Myopia and hypermetropia", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce4a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce4b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e1"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52a3"], "question": {"text": "For an object placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;from a lens, a sharp focused image is observed on a screen placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;from the lens. A glass plate of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;is introduced between lens and screen such that the glass plate plane faces parallel to the screen. By what distance should the object be shifted so that a sharp focused image is observed again on the screen?"}, "options": [{"id": "104b6e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce4c"}, {"id": "f51c87", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce4d"}, {"id": "8fd8cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce4e"}, {"id": "67c20e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce4f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce50", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f39"], "concepts": ["6176f3f76581241c7072b25c"], "question": {"text": "A convex mirror of radius of curvature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math> forms an image that is half the size of the object. The object distance is :"}, "options": [{"id": "5d5390", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce51"}, {"id": "736223", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce52"}, {"id": "9e67af", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce53"}, {"id": "881ece", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce54"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce55", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f3b"], "concepts": ["617aa9daef3fe65ad8e829f4"], "question": {"text": "An object is placed at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> in front of a plane mirror. The virtual and erect image is formed by the mirror. Now the mirror is moved by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> towards the stationary object. The distance by which the position of image would be shifted, will be"}, "options": [{"id": "3070a6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> towards mirror", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce56"}, {"id": "edd9c3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> towards mirror", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce57"}, {"id": "f232b0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> away from mirror", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce58"}, {"id": "33de88", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> towards mirror", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce59"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce5a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["6162fb4c6ed13040ec84d408"], "question": {"text": "What is the relative decrease in focal length of a lens for an increase in optical power by 0.1 D from 2.5D ? ['D' stands for dioptre]"}, "options": [{"id": "b7848c", "text": "$0.01$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce5b"}, {"id": "948a2d", "text": "$0.04$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce5c"}, {"id": "c6357b", "text": "$0.40$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce5d"}, {"id": "61dd77", "text": "$0.1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce5e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce5f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538326"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b565e"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement I : When the white light passed through a prism, the red light bends lesser than yellow and violet.\nStatement II : The refractive indices are different for different wavelengths in dispersive medium. In the light of the above statements, chose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "7b9fb3", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce60"}, {"id": "e6f282", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce61"}, {"id": "15c6e6", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce62"}, {"id": "4bb308", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce63"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce64", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b474f"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b22"], "question": {"text": "The value of numerical aperture of the objective lens of a microscope is <math><mn>1.25</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If light of wavelength <math><mn>5000</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#8491;</mi></math> is used, the minimum separation between two points, to be seen as distinct, will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "e36c8b", "text": "<math><mn>0.48</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce65"}, {"id": "e67501", "text": "<math><mn>0.24</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce66"}, {"id": "9ef64b", "text": "<math><mn>0.38</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce67"}, {"id": "e1175c", "text": "<math><mn>0.12</mn><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce68"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce69", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4756"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4708"], "question": {"text": "<p>The speed of light in media <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively. A ray of light enters from the medium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;at an incident angle<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>. If the ray suffers total internal reflection, then</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "77d293", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce6a"}, {"id": "e8e320", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce6b"}, {"id": "8d836d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce6c"}, {"id": "a303f6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce6d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce6e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa023"], "question": {"text": "A ray of laser of a wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>630</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> is incident at an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at the diamond-air interface. It is going from diamond to air. The refractive index of diamond is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>42</mn></math> and that of air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Choose the correct option."}, "options": [{"id": "d99ede", "text": "Angle of refraction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce6f"}, {"id": "c6584d", "text": "Angle of refraction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce70"}, {"id": "ad8928", "text": "Refraction is not possible.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce71"}, {"id": "7d3dca", "text": "Angle of refraction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>53</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce72"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce73", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e1"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52a3"], "question": {"text": "A symmetric thin biconvex lens is cut into four equal parts by two planes $A B$ and $C D$ as shown in figure. If the power of original lens is 4 D then the power of a part of the divided lens is\n\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FaJA3Zy3AypzE0R8yLUg_XnUFL27c5qXveOsWmxbnPDs.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "816794", "text": "D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce74"}, {"id": "09e102", "text": "8D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce75"}, {"id": "48a5a5", "text": "2D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce76"}, {"id": "1c2823", "text": "4D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce77"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce78", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f39"], "concepts": ["6162fb486ed13040ec84d13d"], "question": {"text": "A concave mirror has radius of curvature of <math><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> It is at the bottom of a glass that has water filled up to <math><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> (see figure). If a small particle is floating on the surface of water, its image as seen, from directly above the glass, is at a distance <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> from the surface of water. The value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> is close to: (Refractive index of water <math><mo>=</mo><mn>1.33</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe660bd30-44a2-40db-8815-119fc7ba5e8e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 194px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "2e9807", "text": "<math><mn>13.4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce79"}, {"id": "9fe355", "text": "<math><mn>8.8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce7a"}, {"id": "62e5e6", "text": "<math><mn>6.7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce7b"}, {"id": "9765c4", "text": "<math><mn>11.7&nbsp;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce7c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce7d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b30"], "question": {"text": "A double convex lens has power&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;and same radii of curvature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math>&nbsp;of both the surfaces. The radius of curvature of a surface of a plano-convex lens made of the same material with power&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;is :"}, "options": [{"id": "99214b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce7e"}, {"id": "44f1bd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce7f"}, {"id": "844279", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce80"}, {"id": "13c217", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce81"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce82", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b565d"], "question": {"text": "A microscope is focused on an object at the bottom of a bucket. If liquid with refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is poured inside the bucket, then microscope have to be raised by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mi>cm</mi></math> to focus the object again. The height of the liquid in the bucket is :"}, "options": [{"id": "6eb28f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce83"}, {"id": "ed9b7a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce84"}, {"id": "8145f0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce85"}, {"id": "447a3b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dce86"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:35.684Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:35.684Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dced5"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dced3", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dceb7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5677"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa023"], "question": {"text": "<p>In a medium the speed of light wave decreases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;times to its speed in free space. The ratio of relative permittivity to the refractive index of the medium is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is ______.</p><p>(Given speed of light in free space <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and for the given medium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "fe97e6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dceb8"}, {"id": "fe4a37", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dceb9"}, {"id": "17fddf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dceba"}, {"id": "7ad93d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcebb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcebc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4755"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9250"], "question": {"text": "The distance between object and its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> times magnified virtual image as produced by a convex lens is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The focal length of the lens used is ________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "ce8e79", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcebd"}, {"id": "058b2a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcebe"}, {"id": "f38daa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcebf"}, {"id": "53b26a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e1"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52a3"], "question": {"text": "A convex lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is placed in front of convex mirror with principal axis coinciding each other. The distance between the lens and mirror is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. A point object is placed on principal axis at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from the convex lens. The image formed by combination coincides the object itself. The focal length of the convex mirror is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "7ff051", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec2"}, {"id": "c665b2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec3"}, {"id": "ae9e9d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec4"}, {"id": "957582", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60da9b4f62f042332c538326"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f925c"], "question": {"text": "A ray of light passing through a prism&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;suffers minimum deviation. It is found that the angle of incidence is double the angle of refraction within the prism. Then, the angle of prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"bottom\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></menclose></math>&nbsp;(in degrees)."}, "options": [{"id": "64a73f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec7"}, {"id": "3aceb1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec8"}, {"id": "61a638", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcec9"}, {"id": "cfb056", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dceca"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcecb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60da9b5062f042332c538358"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f39"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c2"], "question": {"text": "Distance between object and its image $\\left( \\text{magnified by } -\\frac{1}{3}\\right)$ is 30 cm. The focal length of the mirror used is $\\left(\\frac{x}{4}\\right) \\mathrm{cm}$,<br/>where magnitude of value of $x$ is _________."}, "options": [{"id": "16a964", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcecc"}, {"id": "4cff6e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcecd"}, {"id": "f61691", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcece"}, {"id": "7a889f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4f5dcf815cd79dcecf"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:35.778Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:35.778Z", "__v": 0}, "position":